# the external flash at 0x70200000.  Everything above CONFIG_RAM_END is
# therefore owned by the NPU, which means the NuttX image must stay below the
# 2MB mark: this configuration is deliberately minimal (no LVGL, no camera,
# no framebuffer -- the 768KB LTDC framebuffer alone would not fit) and is
# meant for NPU bring-up, while the "nsh" configuration keeps the full
# application.
#
# Flash layout used with this configuration:
#   0x70000000  FSBL (32KB)
#   0x70200000  ATON model initializers (network-data.hex of the ST example)
#   0x70800000  NuttX image (EXTMEM_LRUN_SOURCE_ADDRESS in the FSBL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Camera -> NPU pose estimation (r36): the same NPU stack as configs/npu plus
# the IMX335/DCMIPP capture path (frame lands in the LTDC framebuffer) and the
# pose_cam test, which converts it to the model input and decodes the result.
CONFIG_VIDEO_STREAM=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_POSE_CAM=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_POSE_CAM_STACKSIZE=8192
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_PALM_CAM=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_EYE_GUIDE=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_EYE_CAM=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_EYE_CAM_STACKSIZE=8192
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_PALM_CAM_STACKSIZE=8192
# Stretch the frame into the 192x192 input (r62 behaviour).  Measured on the
# same frame, the reference model scores logit +2.49 with this layout against
# +0.86 with ST's 192x115 letterbox; the board's own implementation differs
# from the reference by up to ~3.5 logits, so the letterbox margin sits below
# that noise floor and palm detections flipped to "no palm".
# CONFIG_EXAMPLES_PALM_CAM_LETTERBOX is not set
############################################################################
