The DMA driver could already do peripheral-to-memory (the ADC uses it), with
the source fixed and the destination incrementing.  Playback is the mirror
image: memory increments, the peripheral stays put, and the peripheral is the
destination rather than the source.  Three register fields differ, so this
adds one function rather than a second driver.

The SAI had an input path only.  Output is the same registers in the other
direction: master transmitter instead of master receiver, MCLK driven out for
the codec instead of ignored, and the data register written instead of read.
