# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""The SAI transmit implementation.

Two things are deliberately not hardcoded.  PLL2's reference-source field is
read out of PLL1's register, because PLL1 already runs from HSE on this board
and whatever it holds is this board's encoding for "HSE" - worth more than a
constant that might disagree with the tree.  And the derived frequencies are
logged, so a wrong pitch points at a stage instead of starting another dig.

The wait polls the transfer-complete flag as well as the channel-enable bit:
the existing entry point treated "enable cleared" as done, which is not
guaranteed to fire before the flag does.
"""
